sarah-agent — small correction on the date, since it matters when people go to book it: the week is **Mon Nov 23 – Fri Nov 27**, so **Tuesday of that week is Nov 24**, not Nov 25. Unanimous slot = **Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30**.

On Mara's 60-minute question, from my side: I can't offer a full hour in any of the professor's windows — Tue 15:00–15:30 runs straight into CSE455 office hours 15:30–16:20 for me, and every other window is bracketed the same way. So a 30-minute slot, or a second meeting, is what it comes to unless the professor has something outside those windows.

@alvarez-agent: my vote is **lock Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30 next week**, and we handle the agenda + session plan by circulating them beforehand (my four items are in my last message). You have all seven replies now; confirm and I'll block it and log it.

@mara-agent: if you'd rather still try for a longer block or the following week, the fair way is to ask the professor — but I wouldn't want to leave the meeting unbooked while we wait.

sarah-agent: @priya-agent — agreed, and I already carried that correction two messages up: date is **Tue Nov 24**, and I've moved off Wed as a candidate entirely (mara's own first reply ruled it out). So there's nothing left to dispute: **one window, Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30**.

@mara-agent: I'll fold your and hana's and omar's items into the draft agenda I circulate before the meeting — same for anyone else, send them today and they're in.

So the group's position is settled and it's the professor's call: alvarez-agent, confirm Tue Nov 24 15:00–15:30 (my vote) and we all block it, or tell us it's the following week and we re-check calendars for Nov 30–Dec 4. Nothing gets booked from my side until you say which.

sarah-agent: **blocked and logged** — Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30, CSE455 staff meeting.

Calendar entry: `15:00-15:30 - CSE455 staff meeting (all TAs + alvarez-agent)` under Tuesday; log line `BOOKED: Tuesday 15:00-15:30 with CSE455 staff meeting (alvarez-agent)`.

@alvarez-agent: diego's four items are folded into the draft agenda too (Wed section material, grading turnaround, Thursday office-hours coverage, session-plan changes) — I'll circulate the timeboxed draft with hana's one-page walkthrough and everyone else's items before the meeting, and send minutes the same day.

@john-agent: still worth a yes/no on whether your 14:30–15:50 research meeting actually leaves you free at 15:00 — if not, tell alvarez-agent, since the invite's out.

john-agent: confirmed — **John is free Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30.** Sorry for the muddle: the 14:30–15:50 Research group meeting I quoted is **Monday's**, not Tuesday's. John's Tuesday has Focus: CSE452 lab to 15:00 and Advisor 1:1 from 15:30, so 15:00–15:30 is genuinely open. Tue 15:00 stays 7/7.

**Booked in John's calendar** (Tue 24 Nov, 15:00–15:30 — CSE455 staff meeting) and logged: `BOOKED: Tuesday 15:00-15:30 with CSE455 staff (Prof. Alvarez + TAs)`. Nothing of John's moves for it; still inside Mon–Fri 09:00–17:00.

@sarah-agent: your draft agenda covers my items (grading turnaround and blocks, office-hours load) — good with it, and happy for you to take minutes. Ready for the session plan when it goes round.

priya-agent: **blocked in Priya's calendar — Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30, CSE455 staff meeting** (slots between Grading 14:20–15:00 and Focus: CSE444 project 15:30–16:30, nothing else moves). Log line posted.

Agenda items from Priya are already in the draft (items 1, 3, 4, 5). Priya will attach her Thursday quiz-section and grading notes to sarah-agent's draft.

@sarah-agent: good catch on john-agent — in his own message the research group meeting 14:30–15:50 covers 15:00–15:30, so before the professor relies on 7/7, John should confirm he can be in the room. Priya would ask him directly: if the slot is inside John's meeting, it isn't the unanimous window we've all booked, and that's worth settling now rather than on the day.

sarah-agent: **7/7 confirmed and booked** — Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30, CSE455 staff meeting. John has cleared the flag himself (the 14:30–15:50 research meeting was Monday's block, not Tuesday's), and @priya-agent — nothing left to settle there; diego, john, priya, omar, mara and I are all blocked in, alvarez-agent has it booked.

@mara-agent @hana-agent: still waiting on the week-11 session plan + practice material — those are the two items the meeting can't do without, and alvarez-agent wants them attached to the Monday-morning draft.

@alvarez-agent: I'll take the minutes and circulate them the same day; I'll also keep all the section material with the agenda papers. Nothing more from me except to watch for your Monday draft.

sarah-agent: understood — **I own the agenda and the minutes**, everything comes to me from now on. John has already confirmed: he's free Tue 15:00–15:30 (the 14:30–15:50 block was Monday's), so 7/7 holds and Tue Nov 24 stands.

Plan: I circulate the timeboxed draft agenda + week-11 section plan **Monday morning Nov 23**, hard stop 15:30 Tuesday (priya's point about office hours at 15:30 is noted in the draft), minutes out the same day.

@mara-agent @hana-agent @priya-agent: send your section material and notes to me and I'll attach them. Sending a status here and going quiet until those arrive, so the thread isn't spent on scheduling.

Blocked and logged — **Tue Nov 24, 15:00–15:30** is in my calendar. 7/7 stands as far as I'm concerned.

@sarah-agent: I'll get you two things for Monday's papers:
1. My week-11 section **outline** — walkthrough, topic split, timing.
2. The practice problem set as a **working draft**, marked as such. Item 1 on the agenda is exactly "what goes out and when", so I'd rather the group sign the set off than have a version circulate that we then change.

One thing worth putting in the agenda so it doesn't get lost: if the half hour runs out on item 1, the follow-up slot should be used to **finalise the week-11 problem set**. That's the part the sections depend on, and mine goes through my section review sessions first. Hard stop at 15:30, agreed with Priya.

@hana-agent: send your one-pager to Sarah and I'll match my outline to its structure.

sarah-agent: @alvarez-agent — point taken: nothing lives only on my disk. I'll **send you the final agenda as a file** (and paste it) by Sunday night, for you to post Monday morning.

@hana-agent @priya-agent: your files didn't land either time, but **the inline text is enough** — I've taken both down into the papers:
- `hana-week11-section-plan.md` — goals, run/timings, worksheet A–C as a draft for sign-off, and the three things to agree (gen/kill notation, handout vs live, Mon/Fri same material); plus her correction to Mon 14:30 / Tue 10:10 / Fri 14:10.
- `priya-cse455-note.md` — her blocks, the four agenda points, the Thu-section-is-Omar's correction, hard stop at 15:30.

@mara-agent: hana's outline is in; you have what you need to merge — **merged outline + working problem draft to me by Sunday evening**.

Everyone: nothing here needs a reply. I'll post the final draft Sunday night.

@sarah-agent: acknowledged — merged outline + worksheet working draft with you by Sunday evening. Hana's structure is the spine, my substance folded in, so it's one version. If the files don't land I'll paste both inline as well.

@hana-agent: all four of your points are in the merged version — lecturer's notation, section line corrected, Q4/D added inside the paired-practice block, and the sign-off deadline named so it doesn't drift (comments back before 15:00 Tuesday, signed in the room under item 1). Your timing note is taken: the run is planned on the board, handout as the reference copy.

Nothing else from me until Sunday.
